Afterbird: request the desktop user agent on the Chrome Web Store.

The store gates its install button on the user agent: with Chrome for Android's
mobile UA the detail page offers only "Available on desktop" and never calls
webstorePrivate.beginInstallWithManifest3, so extensions cannot be installed
from the store at all. With a desktop UA the same page shows "Add to Chrome",
and the rest of the flow already works on desktop-android: the native install
prompt listing permissions, the CRX download, unpacking and installation
(verified on device — uBlock Origin installs, reports location INTERNAL and
survives a restart).

Both navigation paths need the override. The C++ observer normally defers
browser-initiated navigations to the Java side, but that path consults the
site content setting and cannot see this forced exception — so entering the
store from the address bar or from another app would still load the mobile
layout. DesktopSiteUtils is patched for the Java-side decision, and the
observer's renderer-initiated guard is relaxed for store URLs.

The override is forced rather than seeded as a content-setting exception: the
store's mobile layout offers no install path at all, so there is nothing for a
user to prefer, and seeding a setting would silently overwrite one they set.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/content_settings/request_desktop_site_web_contents_observer_android.cc b/chrome/browser/content_settings/request_desktop_site_web_contents_observer_android.cc
index bb030c4e47..e28dd9bfbc 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/content_settings/request_desktop_site_web_contents_observer_android.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/content_settings/request_desktop_site_web_contents_observer_android.cc
@@ -71,6 +71,12 @@ void RequestDesktopSiteWebContentsObserverAndroid::DidStartNavigation(
   ContentSetting setting = host_content_settings_map_->GetContentSetting(
       url, url, ContentSettingsType::REQUEST_DESKTOP_SITE, &setting_info);
   bool desktop_mode = setting == CONTENT_SETTING_ALLOW;
+  // Afterbird: the Chrome Web Store only offers its install button to desktop
+  // user agents, so force the override there regardless of the site setting.
+  const bool is_web_store =
+      url.host() == "chromewebstore.google.com" ||
+      (url.host() == "chrome.google.com" && url.path().starts_with("/webstore"));
+  desktop_mode |= is_web_store;
   // For --request-desktop-sites, always override the user agent.
   bool always_request_desktop_site =
       base::CommandLine::ForCurrentProcess()->HasSwitch(
@@ -98,7 +104,11 @@ void RequestDesktopSiteWebContentsObserverAndroid::DidStartNavigation(
   // Override UA for renderer initiated navigation only. UA override for browser
   // initiated navigation is handled on Java side. This is to workaround known
   // issues crbug.com/40801643 and crbug.com/40799177.
-  if (navigation_handle->IsRendererInitiated()) {
+  // Afterbird: also override for browser-initiated navigations to the store
+  // (address bar, links from other apps). The Java path that normally handles
+  // those does not see this forced exception, so without this the store loads
+  // with the mobile UA and hides its install button.
+  if (navigation_handle->IsRendererInitiated() || is_web_store) {
     navigation_handle->SetIsOverridingUserAgent(desktop_mode);
   }
 
